      "text": "Command 0x80061001: Initiate Remote Shell The Initiate Remote Shell command takes a single argument which contains the full filename and path to the command interpreter (e.g. cmd.exe) to use for the remote shell. Once activated, the command handler terminates any existing remote shell processes and closes any open pipes going to the remote shell process. The handler then creates new pipes before generating a new remote shell process and using the newly created pipes for the STDIN , STDOUT and STDERR of the console process. If the CreateProcess call returns an error, the command handler will generate a response with the following fields within the CommandData set:",
